27. The deepest mental model
I want you to think of resilience mechanisms as control systems.
Retry:
observe failure
     ↓
inject another request
Backoff:
observe repeated failure
     ↓
reduce retry frequency
Jitter:
observe correlated behavior
     ↓
desynchronize clients
Retry budget:
observe excessive retry traffic
     ↓
limit amplification
Circuit breaker:
observe persistent failure
     ↓
stop sending traffic
Bulkhead:
observe resource contention
     ↓
isolate resources
Rate limiter:
observe excessive incoming demand
     ↓
control admission
Timeout:
observe excessive waiting
     ↓
release resources / stop waiting
This is much more useful than memorizing five patterns.
