A particularly valuable metric:
retry_success_rate
Suppose:
100,000 retries
and:
200 succeeded
That's:
0.2%
Your retry mechanism is probably generating enormous waste.
If:
100,000 retries
produce:
80,000 successes
then retries may be highly valuable.
So don't ask:
"Do retries exist?"
Ask:
"Are retries buying enough successful work to justify the additional load?"
