3.5 Why INCR is important
Suppose two application servers execute:
Server A → read counter
Server B → read counter
Both see:
100
Then:
A → 101
B → 101
You lost an increment.
This is the classic:
Read
Modify
Write
race.
Redis provides:
INCR counter
as an atomic command from the client's perspective.
Conceptually:
Client A ----\
              \
               Redis event loop
              /
Client B ----/

        INCR
          |
          +-- atomic command execution
This connects directly back to Topic 01: Event Loop + command execution.
