3.43 Complexity — very important for system design
You should know the broad complexity characteristics.
Structure	Typical operation
String GET	O(1)
String SET	O(1) for normal cases
List push/pop ends	O(1)
List indexed lookup	O(N)
Set membership	O(1) average
Hash field lookup	O(1) average
Sorted Set lookup/ranking	typically O(log N) for indexed operations
But there is a critical warning:
Never memorize only "Redis is O(1)."
Some commands depend on:
number of elements
range size
serialization size
data structure
operation type
For example:
HGETALL user:101
is not simply "O(1)" because Redis must return all fields.
Similarly:
LRANGE mylist 0 100000
has work proportional to the amount of data returned.
And:
SMEMBERS hugeSet
can be expensive for a huge Set.
This matters because Redis has a largely single-threaded command execution model: one expensive command can delay other clients.
