56. Cache Stampede
Now we're reaching the final concept from your image.
Suppose:
Product:123
TTL = 60 seconds
Thousands of users request it.
While alive:
Request
   ↓
Redis
   ↓
cache hit
Very efficient.
But suddenly:
TTL expires
Now thousands of requests arrive simultaneously:
Request 1 ─┐
Request 2 ─┤
Request 3 ─┤
Request 4 ─┤
Request 5 ─┤
...        ├──→ Redis MISS
Request N ─┘
              ↓
          DB/database
Now all requests may hit the database.
This is:
Cache Stampede
Also called:
Cache Avalanche
depending on the exact scenario/usage of the term.
