58. Why TTL Randomization Helps
Suppose you cache:
1 million products
and accidentally assign:
TTL = 3600
to all of them at the same time.
Then:
T = 0
  ↓
all inserted

T = 3600
  ↓
many expire together
Bad.
Instead use jitter:
TTL = 3600 + random(0..300)
So:
product A → 3621 sec
product B → 3740 sec
product C → 3688 sec
product D → 3892 sec
