2. Distributed lock
Only one request rebuilds the cache:
Request A
   ↓
cache miss
   ↓
acquire lock
   ↓
load DB
   ↓
populate Redis
   ↓
release lock
Other requests wait or use stale data.
________________________________________
3. Request coalescing / single-flight
Multiple requests for the same key share one refresh operation.
Conceptually:
100 requests
     ↓
same missing key
     ↓
one DB request
     ↓
result shared
________________________________________
4. Stale-while-revalidate
Serve slightly stale data while one process refreshes the cache.
cached value
     ↓
slightly stale
     ↓
serve old value
     +
background refresh
This is often excellent for high-read systems.
