38. One level deeper: replication is a stream, not a snapshot
This is the mental shift I want you to make.
Don't visualize:
Primary
   |
   | "copy my database"
   v
Replica
Visualize:
Primary
   |
   | continuous stream of changes
   v
Replica
Then:
offset
tells us:
"How far through the stream has the replica progressed?"
And:
backlog
tells us:
"How much recent stream history can the primary still provide?"
And:
