37. Interview-Level Questions You Should Be Able to Answer
Don't move on from Sentinel until you can reason through these.
Q1
Why do we need Sentinel if Redis already has replication?
Expected reasoning:
Replication = redundant copies

Sentinel = failure detection + automated failover +
           master discovery
________________________________________
Q2
What's the difference between SDOWN and ODOWN?
SDOWN = one Sentinel thinks node is unavailable

ODOWN = enough Sentinels agree that master is unavailable
________________________________________
Q3
What's the difference between quorum and majority?
Quorum → determines ODOWN

Majority → gives failover authorization
________________________________________
Q4
Can Sentinel guarantee zero data loss?
No.
Because:
Redis replication = asynchronous
An acknowledged write may not have reached the promoted replica.
________________________________________
Q5
What happens when the old master returns?
It is reconfigured as a replica of the new master.
________________________________________
Q6
Is Sentinel a proxy?
No.
It is primarily a control-plane/discovery/failover component.
________________________________________
Q7
Does Sentinel shard Redis?
No.
Sentinel provides HA/failover.
Redis Cluster provides sharding + HA.
