11.18 What if the failed node comes back?
This is another useful scenario.
Suppose:
P2 crashes
R2 becomes primary
Then P2 comes back online.
It cannot simply say:
"I'm back, give me my slots."
The cluster's authoritative state has changed.
P2 is now effectively a node that needs to synchronize with the new topology/state.
Conceptually:
Old:

P2 = primary
R2 = replica


After failover:

R2 = primary
P2 = old primary
P2 can be reconfigured to replicate from the new primary.
So eventually:
R2 = primary
P2 = replica
This is an important operational pattern:
Failover changes roles; recovery doesn't necessarily restore the old roles.
