application threads
       ↓
waiting
       ↓
thread pool exhaustion
So:
Redis latency can indirectly become Java thread-pool exhaustion.
This is why connection-pool metrics belong in your Redis monitoring dashboard.
________________________________________
14.28 Failure mode #12 — Retry + connection pool feedback loop
Here's a nasty production cascade.
Initial:
Redis latency ↑
Then:
requests hold connections longer
Then:
connection pool exhausted
Then:
requests timeout
Then:
application retries
Then:
more Redis traffic
Then:
Redis latency ↑↑
Full loop:
Redis slow
   ↓
connections occupied
   ↓
pool exhausted
   ↓
timeouts
   ↓
retries
   ↓
more load
   ↓
Redis even slower
This is a positive feedback loop.
A good architecture breaks it with:
