15. Why "invalidate everything immediately" isn't trivial
Imagine you have:
10,000 application instances
and a product changes.
You could theoretically broadcast:
INVALIDATE product:123
to everybody.
But now you have another distributed-system problem:
Did every node receive the invalidation?
Suppose:
App #1 ✓
App #2 ✓
App #3 ✓
App #4 ✗
App #5 ✓
...
App #4 continues serving stale data.
What if App #4 was temporarily disconnected?
What if it crashed?
What if the message was lost?
What if it received the event twice?
What if events arrive out of order?
Now cache invalidation becomes an event delivery + ordering + failure recovery problem.
