37. The full progression so far
You can now see why we're studying these lessons in this order.
Lesson 1
We discovered:
Caching creates multiple copies.
Therefore:
copies can become stale.
Lesson 2
We discovered:
TTL
handles uncertainty through time.
And:
explicit invalidation
handles known mutations.
Lesson 3
Now:
multiple application instances
mean invalidation itself must propagate through a distributed system.
So we need:
events
durability
replay
idempotency
ordering
versioning
